# Identity Layer

## Overview

The **Identity Layer** defines the foundational identity of the **A01 Blockchain Intelligence Agent** within the CIE-OS ecosystem.

This layer contains the architectural contracts that describe **what the agent is, why it exists, what responsibilities it owns, and what boundaries it must never cross.**

No production logic, business rules, blockchain processing, or implementation code belongs in this layer.

Instead, this layer acts as the permanent reference for every future development phase.

---

# Purpose

The Identity Layer exists to answer the following questions before any code is written:

* What is this agent?
* Why does it exist?
* What problems does it solve?
* What are its responsibilities?
* What are its limitations?
* How should the rest of the CIE-OS ecosystem interact with it?
* How will success be measured?

---

# Design Philosophy

The A01 Blockchain Intelligence Agent follows a **Documentation-First Engineering** approach.

Architecture is defined before implementation.

Responsibilities are defined before features.

Interfaces are defined before integrations.

Code must always implement documented behavior—not redefine it.

---

# Identity Documents

This folder contains the following documents.

| Document            | Purpose                                       |
| ------------------- | --------------------------------------------- |
| agent_profile.md    | Official identity of the agent                |
| mission.md          | Vision, mission and long-term purpose         |
| objectives.md       | Measurable objectives                         |
| scope.md            | Functional boundaries                         |
| responsibilities.md | Agent responsibilities                        |
| capabilities.md     | Complete capability catalogue                 |
| limitations.md      | Known limitations and non-goals               |
| architecture.md     | High-level intelligence architecture          |
| lifecycle.md        | Runtime lifecycle                             |
| interfaces.md       | Internal and external communication contracts |
| glossary.md         | Official terminology                          |
| success_criteria.md | Definition of success                         |

---

# Development Rules

The Identity Layer is considered a **Design Contract**.

Every future module must remain compatible with these documents.

No implementation is allowed to contradict this layer without updating the corresponding design document first.

